 a pump that should default off.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.55\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"wrong_component_type\",\n      \"components\": [\"C5\", \"C4\", \"R9\", \"R6\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"C5.1\", \"C5.2\", \"C4.1\", \"C4.2\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"FLOAT_HIGH\", \"FLOAT_LOW\", \"+3V3\", \"GND\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The filter capacitor on the high float input, C5, is connected between FLOAT_HIGH and +3V3. The matching filter on the low float input, C4, is connected between FLOAT_LOW and GND. The two float-input filters are therefore not configured the same way.\",\n      \"expected\": \"Both float-switch input filters should return to GND, consistent with the other filter (C4) and with R9, which pulls FLOAT_HIGH to GND.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"74\\\") (name \\\"FLOAT_HIGH\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"C5\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\")) ...\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"75\\\") (name \\\"FLOAT_LOW\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"C4\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\")) ...\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"C5 FLOAT_HIGH +3V3 100n\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"C4 0 FLOAT_LOW 100n\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The high-float input has its filter returned to the 3.3 V rail, not to ground. This gives weaker noise filtering on the float-switch signal and a different level-reference behaviour from the low-float input, which may cause spurious high-level readings or overflow-interlock false triggers.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The most likely anomaly is R5 pulling the main-pump MOSFET gate up to +3V3 instead of down to GND, which would leave the pump on by default unlike the ATO stage. A weaker secondary concern is that the FLOAT_HIGH filter capacitor C5 returns to +3V3 while its low-side counterpart returns to GND.\"\n}",
